Balance and lifecycle rules
- Every active method is displayed even if it has no transactions; show ৳0.00 and a prompt to set an opening balance if appropriate.
- Adding a method must not change existing balances.
- Renaming a method updates its displayed name but does not rewrite historical transaction values if records store snapshots; stable method IDs should resolve to the current label for normal display, while archived historical labels remain readable.
- A method with historical activity cannot be hard-deleted. Archive it and prevent new selection; keep old records and reports readable.
- Built-in methods cannot be removed or duplicated.
- The user's opening balance for a new method is a separate setup entry/state, not income.
- A credit card needs a carefully defined balance convention (e.g. positive available funds versus amount owed). Do not treat credit card liability as ordinary cash without an explicit model. If credit cards are included in the first release, document the sign and net-worth treatment before implementation.
