22. Final Product Idea
EcO should become a single, reliable daily money companion. The user records any financial activity through one consistent Add flow; understands all activity in one List; sees balances separated by account and by financial position; learns from Statistics without being shamed; and manages their own preferences in Settings. People who do not use EcO remain supported through local ledgers and carefully scoped share links, while EcO users can create mutual connections and approve shared transactions.

The most important order of work is:
1. Protect existing data first through a versioned JSON backup and verified import.
2. Unify entry and history so the app feels simple and consistent.
3. Centralize payment-method configuration without breaking old balances.
4. Prove all financial calculations with regression tests.
5. Add cross-account sharing only with trusted authorization and scheduling, because mistakes here can affect another person's financial records.
The guiding promise should be: “Record money simply. Understand it clearly. Keep your data safe. Share only what you choose.”
Blueprint update: reminders and inbox
The Transactions experience includes an optional, user-reviewed WhatsApp reminder for a person who is not mutually connected on EcO. The application shell includes a notification bell/inbox for every signed-in user, with automatic deletion after seven days. See Sections 2.4, 15, and 17 for the exact legacy backup contract, message flow, privacy constraints, and retention requirements.
23. Authoritative UI Design System — Institutional Emerald
