23.1 Design language
- Product style: Institutional Emerald — dark-first, restrained, high-trust fintech terminal.
- Dark-only. <html class="dark">. Do not create a light theme, light-theme tokens, or a theme switch.
- No pure black or pure white. Use layered charcoal surfaces.
- Emerald is the primary/action and positive semantic accent. Salmon is negative/error. Slate-blue/gray is neutral transfer. Pending uses a restrained tertiary treatment. Everything else is grayscale surface tiers.
- Use high information density only where it genuinely helps (for example, transaction history), while maintaining consistent spacing and strong visual hierarchy.
- Avoid decorative gradients, large empty hero areas, unnecessary illustrations, glowing effects, oversized cards, and repeated explanatory copy.
